Why? It has a very useful gameplay effect: it discourages people from
finding a level where weak, large, edible monsters (e.g. rothes) are
generated fast enough to avoid starvation, and camping out there killing
same indefinitely.  (Angband is susceptible to a similar tactic: get 
Satisfy Hunger and the Phial, and you can farm your chosen safe depth
(500', say) until you find Ringil, the One Ring, Bladeturner, and the
Helm of Dor-Lomin. Assuming you don't die of boredom, and your computer's
CPU doesn't go berserk from a high-energy cosmic ray impact.)

If you adopt this tactic in Nethack, you will suddenly find that you're
now getting mumakil instead of rothes, and that your armour class is
utterly inadequate for stopping a mumak from flattening you.  If, on
the other hand, you press onwards into the dungeon, you will find new
levels, with more equipment in them.

If you want Angband, you know where to get it :)

